// gs_set writes one `mb` slot. lset is the generic "store into a list
// element" helper demos/moonbuggy/engine/core/core-1/cell/cell.id explains:
// an imported list cannot be index-assigned directly, but passing it as a
// parameter makes the lvalue an identifier again, and lists are
// reference-semantic so the store is shared. world/game/state/rng reuses
// this same lset for its own one-cell PRNG state.

gs_set(int i, int v) {
  lset((import mb), i, v);
} return void;

lset(int[] xs, int i, int v) {
  xs[i] = v;
} return void;
